body:
Thank you Stof. i don't know if it's a common bad value, but, we should fix that in **getClientIps** as i suggested. The problem is not closely to '**uknown**' value, we can get any other bad value. The right way is to check the value extracted from x-forwarded-for if it's not a valid IP, we should use the REMOTE_ADDR.

Here is what i did in my service:

```
$ip = $this->request->getClientIp();

        //@see: https://github.com/symfony/symfony/issues/15525
        if(!$this->isValidPublicIP($ip)){ // check if the IP given by Sf Request is good. Otherwise, use the Native PHP REMOTE_ADDR
            $this->log(sprintf("Bad IP from SF: %s. Try the Remote ADDR\n", $ip));
            $ip = $this->request->server->get('REMOTE_ADDR');
        }

        if (!$this->isValidPublicIP($ip)) { // This is a seconf check. If does not pass,... there is a problem
            $this->log(sprintf("Not valid IP: %s \n", $ip));
            return null;
        }
```

I hope this code can give an idea to fix this issue.
